.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt LCC-SESSION 1
.Os @PROJECT_VERSION@

.Sh NAME
.Nm lcc-session
.Nd configure general Lumina session options.

.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | -help
.Op Fl v | -version

.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is part of the Lumina Control Center.
It sets general options for the Lumina session:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Window manager to run in the session.
.It
Time and date display formats, and the order in which they are shown.
A sample of each format is displayed, and the valid format codes can be
viewed from the window.
An empty format uses the short format of the current locale.
.It
Whether Num Lock is enabled at login.
.It
Whether the login and logout sounds are played.
.It
Whether application crash data is shown.
When enabled,
.Xr lumina-open 1
watches the processes it starts and reports those that fail.
.It
Whether desktop links are managed automatically for installed applications.
.It
Whether startup quotes are disabled.
.It
The user icon shown at login.
The selected image is scaled to 64x64 pixels.
.El
.Pp
Desktop settings can also be reset, either to the system defaults
(including operating system customizations) or to the plain Lumina
defaults.
A confirmation is requested before either reset.

.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display help on command line options.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Display version information.
.El

.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/lcc-session
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lumina-desktop/sessionsettings.conf
Session settings.
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lumina-desktop/nowatch
Present when application crash data is disabled.
.It Pa ~/.loginIcon.png
User icon.
.El

.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lcc 1 ,
.Xr lcc-locale 1 ,
.Xr lcc-sound-theme 1 ,
.Xr lumina-desktop 1

